// A line with `fn` in the body of a `{` that is never closed, indented deeper than the line of the `{`. A deeper item word does
// not end the unit (§18.1), so the `{` is what is reported, with the item after it or without (D2).
// The unit ends at the item that follows it, on a line with the same or a shallower indentation. A bracket that is not closed
// is reported whatever stopped the reading: the E0002 points at the innermost bracket that is not closed (§18.1, S-943,
// R-371). The same file without the item after the unit is unclosed_eof_d2_fn.onsa, and the report is on the same line.

fn a() -> I32 {                                 //~ E0002 @15
  1
    fn k() -> I32 { 2 }
fn c() -> I32 { 3 }
